WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.068 --> 00:00:15.959
Sage peeled a banana—her favorite after-practice snack—as she and her best friend, Lourdes, walked out of Park Gymnastics.

2
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:23.243
"I can't believe the tryouts for Misty Blackwell's Gymnastics Camp are next Saturday," Sage said.

3
00:00:23.244 --> 00:00:30.791
For three years in a row, she had tried out for the camp run by former Olympian Misty Blackwell.

4
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:36.727
But Misty, a six-time gold medalist, only chose gymnasts with Olympic potential.

5
00:00:36.728 --> 00:00:42.411
Since Sage's last rejection, she had been preparing for this year's tryouts.

6
00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:49.899
Her parents thought she put too much pressure on herself, but going to the Olympics had been Sage's dream forever.

7
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.615
"I'm so nervous about the tryouts," Lourdes said.

8
00:00:54.616 --> 00:00:58.902
"You're going to make it this year," Sage said firmly.

9
00:00:58.903 --> 00:01:01.909
"You're the best gymnast at Park.

10
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:07.806
Besides, it's our last chance—we'll be too old next year.

11
00:01:07.807 --> 00:01:11.892
Plus, maybe the camp will help us catch up to Emi!" Emi

12
00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:20.339
Wilson was the top gymnast at Park's rival gym and had been to the camp three times already. "There's

13
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:28.172
a rumor that Emi's going to train overseas this summer, so she's not trying out," Lourdes said. Sage's

14
00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:33.536
face lit up. "Really?" She grinned. Emi's

15
00:01:33.537 --> 00:01:39.651
absence this year would definitely give Sage an advantage she had never had before. "I'll

16
00:01:39.652 --> 00:01:46.650
work extra hard this week to get one step closer to my dream!" ***

17
00:01:46.651 --> 00:01:53.187
When Sage and Lourdes arrived at the tryouts, the gym was packed with gymnasts and spectators.

18
00:01:53.188 --> 00:01:59.354
The girls joined the line at the registration table just as Misty Blackwell walked past.

19
00:01:59.355 --> 00:02:02.454
The famous gymnast stopped briefly to greet them.

20
00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:07.387
"I remember you two from last year—good luck with your tryouts."

21
00:02:07.388 --> 00:02:13.463
Sage froze. "Thank you, Ms. Blackwell!"

22
00:02:13.464 --> 00:02:17.147
"She remembered us!" Lourdes said.

23
00:02:17.148 --> 00:02:23.611
"I need to make sure that she remembers my performance too," Sage said.

24
00:02:23.612 --> 00:02:27.814
The girls took their seats and waited for the tryouts to start.

25
00:02:27.815 --> 00:02:33.280
"First up," the announcer called, "Emi Wilson."

26
00:02:33.281 --> 00:02:39.295
Lourdes gasped. "What's she doing here?"

27
00:02:39.296 --> 00:02:45.078
"I guess the rumors were wrong," Sage mumbled.

28
00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:52.488
As Sage watched Emi's performance, she could feel her anxiety mounting—Emi's technique was perfect.

29
00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:55.450
But Sage couldn't let it rattle her.

30
00:02:55.451 --> 00:03:02.098
"If Emi can give a perfect performance, so can you," she told herself sternly.

31
00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:05.295
"You've worked hard all week for this!"

32
00:03:05.296 --> 00:03:12.905
After Emi gave a final bow, the announcer called Sage to the floor.

33
00:03:12.906 --> 00:03:15.759
Lourdes flashed her a sympathetic look.

34
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.757
"It stinks that you have to go right after Emi."

35
00:03:19.758 --> 00:03:22.684
Sage tried to brush it off.

36
00:03:22.685 --> 00:03:28.743
"I'm super prepared—Emi isn't the only one with Olympic potential." "That's

37
00:03:28.744 --> 00:03:35.555
the right attitude!" Lourdes grinned. "Good luck!" Sage

38
00:03:35.556 --> 00:03:40.738
walked onto the mat and breathed in deeply. As

39
00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:48.120
the music started, she raised her arms, striking a pose before tiptoeing backward to the edge of the mat. She

40
00:03:48.121 --> 00:03:54.065
was preparing for her first big move—a series of fast forward flips across the mat. But

41
00:03:54.066 --> 00:04:00.217
something instantly felt wrong . . . Had her last step been too wide? Yes—and

42
00:04:00.218 --> 00:04:04.348
her heel had gone out of bounds! "Such

43
00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:10.497
a stupid mistake!" a voice in her head screamed. Quickly

44
00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:13.914
she tried to reassure herself. "You

45
00:04:13.915 --> 00:04:21.298
can make up for the error. Yesterday at practice your routine was perfect!" With

46
00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:25.617
that, Sage began her running start for the first flip. Suddenly

47
00:04:25.618 --> 00:04:29.509
everything seemed to move in slow motion. Her

48
00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:35.510
right foot wasn't in position . . . her last step was awkward. She

49
00:04:35.511 --> 00:04:38.667
couldn't regain her balance. And

50
00:04:38.668 --> 00:04:44.544
then— bam! Sage flopped facedown onto the mat.

51
00:04:44.545 --> 00:04:49.765
Gasps rose from the crowd, and tears sprang to Sage's eyes.

52
00:04:49.766 --> 00:04:56.241
She wanted to get up and run away, but years of competing had taught her that quitting was not an option.

53
00:04:56.242 --> 00:04:59.807
As she picked herself up, the crowd applauded.

54
00:04:59.808 --> 00:05:06.196
She improvised a few poses, and then bravely continued her routine.

55
00:05:06.197 --> 00:05:12.906
*** After the tryouts Sage sat in a booth at Frosty Spoon, staring at Lourdes'

56
00:05:12.907 --> 00:05:20.164
certificate. Lourdes handed Sage a frozen yogurt, then discreetly slipped the certificate onto the seat, out of Sage's

57
00:05:20.165 --> 00:05:25.227
sight. "Even the best gymnasts fall," Lourdes

58
00:05:25.228 --> 00:05:29.022
said. Sage sighed. "I

59
00:05:29.023 --> 00:05:34.489
know. But even if I hadn't fallen, I wouldn't have gotten into Misty's

60
00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:43.474
camp." "What?" Lourdes said. "But you were so prepared, and you've done so well in competitions this year."

61
00:05:43.475 --> 00:05:53.612
"True," Sage agreed, "but there were lots of amazing gymnasts today—including you—all more talented than I am.

62
00:05:53.613 --> 00:05:59.690
My dream probably wasn't very realistic after all."

63
00:05:59.691 --> 00:06:04.143
"But it's good to dream big!" Lourdes protested.

64
00:06:04.144 --> 00:06:11.421
"Dreams are great," Sage said, "but not all dreams can come true."

65
00:06:11.422 --> 00:06:15.299
"Does this mean you're going to quit gymnastics?"

66
00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:22.237
"I'm not sure what it means yet," Sage said, "but I won't quit."

67
00:06:22.238 --> 00:06:26.770
Lourdes looked sad and uncomfortable.

68
00:06:26.771 --> 00:06:35.581
"I'm disappointed about my poor tryout," Sage added quickly, "but you know what—I'm going to be fine.

69
00:06:35.582 --> 00:06:41.355
Gymnastics might even be more fun without all the pressure I've been putting on myself."

70
00:06:41.356 --> 00:06:44.516
"Good point," Lourdes said.

71
00:06:44.517 --> 00:06:58.183
Sage dipped her spoon into the bowl of frozen yogurt. "Mmm," she said, smiling, "it's my favorite flavor—banana!"

